# InputOtp - the verification code: slots in two groups, a caret, “Verificando…”, ok / bad, a resend countdown. The
# PAGE checks the code: onInput gets it when complete; answer with state ("ok" | "bad") and message.
#   InputOtp(value: code, length: 6, hint: "We sent it to +57 300 123 4567", state: otpState, message: otpMsg, onInput: check)
#   InputOtp(length: 8, letters: true, resendIn: 0, …)   a code copied from another screen (KQ4M-7T2X): letters and
#   digits, in capitals, a pasted dash dropped, and no resend button (resendIn 0 never offers one).
# shadcn-for-muten · Custom (kit values) · host JS input-otp.js.
part InputOtp(value: text = "", length: number = 6, letters: bool = false, hint: text = "", state: text = "", message: text = "", resendIn: number = 30, onInput: action) {
  Custom InputOtp inputs(value: $value, length: $length, letters: $letters, hint: $hint, state: $state, message: $message, resendIn: $resendIn) on(input: $onInput) class("cx-otp-host")
}
